<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maelgwn Gwynedd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 547</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Maglocunus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maelgwn Gwynedd was king of Gwynedd in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> in the 6th century. The writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gildas">Gildas</a> denounced him as Maglocunus, 'dragon of the island', the most powerful of the British kings of his day. He is associated with the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deganwy">Deganwy</a>, and the Welsh annals record his death from the 'yellow plague' around 547.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maelgwn-gwynedd.jpg" alt="Maelgwn Gwynedd" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:History_of_the_Kings_(f.96.v)_Maelgwn_Gwynedd_Detail.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
